   "source": [
    "* In the above function we are calculating the rollin mean and rolling standard devation. for the data.\n",
    "* Given the \"window= 12\" So for every 12 month preiod calculate the mean and std.\n",
    "* And then saving in varible to plot the grpah for rolling mean rolling std and comparing with the original data.\n",
    "* So based on the visuilaztions we can understand that the data is not stationary bcs we can see that the mean is increassng with time while the std devation is increasing slowly.\n",
    "* So for that to confirm with the hypothesis testing that data is not stationary we are using the adfuller test which give cirtical and stats value.\n",
    "* So our stats value is 18.\n",
    "* critical value (alpha) at 5% = -2\n",
    "* So in the hypothesis testing its coming under the graph its confirms data is not stationary\n",
    "*  The adfuller first Value is the Stats Value & the values in the dicstonariy are alph values at 1%,5%,10%.\n",
    "* The function give the ouput in array and dict form. So now for showing that output in proper form saving them in the pd.Series form so the first 4 (0 to 3) values stored with index name given by us mannualy in the series.\n",
    "* So the 4th index in the dictornary so through looping we are saving in the series. storing the key (1% nameing as cirical value) to show with the percentage of Ciritcal value using the \"%s\" so that each value equal to j so means through looping we are adding them in series list one by one in the above graph with the values."
   ]
